{"study_accession":"PRJNA1080008","secondary_study_accession":"SRP491501","title":"Innate immune responses are increased in children with acute asthma exacerbation","description":"Our study aimed to better understand the immune responses during an acute asthma exacerbation in children. Gene expression profiles were examined by RNA-sequencing in blood samples. Samples were collected on average 2.5 day after systemic corticosteroid treatment. Our findings show that pro-inflammatory genes and pathways related to innate responses and signaling remained increased in children hospitalized for acute asthma exacerbation. Genes and pathways involved in adaptive immune respones, particularly T lymphocyte activation, were decreased in children hospitalized for acute asthma exacerbation. These studies suggest that innate immune responses may remain activated following hospitalization for asthma exacerbation. Overall design: Following informed consent, blood samples were collected from patients admitted to hospital for acute asthma exacerbation and healthy controls","pubmed":"38873916","geo_series":"","n_samples":32,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN40097666","study_accession":"PRJNA1080008","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"Pat_20_V_1_34","description":"Pat_20_V_1_34","sex":"female","geo_sample":"GSM8105758","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":2,"first_public":"2024-06-19","attributes":[["source_name","Blood"],["tissue","Blood"],["treatment","Pat"],["age","10"],["sex","female"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR28083126","experiment_accession":"SRX23729749","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":21658099,"base_count":5755993965,"first_public":"2024-06-19","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM8105758: Pat_20_V_1_34 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"},{"run_accession":"SRR28083127","experiment_accession":"SRX23729749","librar